# Caddy — reverse proxy on VM 102
#
# Deployed by ansible/caddy.yml to ~/docker/caddy/Caddyfile.
# This file is the source of truth; the host copy is generated.
#
# The upstream is addressed BY IP, not by hostname. That is deliberate and it
# is what makes the .local -> .internal migration cheap: only the site address
# changes, and Caddy issues a new leaf from the SAME root CA, so no client
# needs to re-trust anything (ARCHITECTURE.md §7.8).
#
# `tls internal` means Caddy's own CA signs this. Adding or changing a
# hostname reuses the existing root; it does not regenerate it.

n8n.leonshomelab.local {
    tls internal
    reverse_proxy 192.168.0.28:5678
}
